WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.460
Glad you're here for unintended consequences, episode 31.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.820
Today's case is a reminder that complex systems

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.340
rarely respond the way we expect them to.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:14.300
In October 1957, the German firm, Hemi Grunenthal,

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.120
began selling Thalidomide across West Germany

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.600
under the name Contrgan.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.180
The company described it as a non-addictive sedative

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:25.200
that could be taken even by pregnant women without risk.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.040
Within four years,

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.560
pediatricians in several countries began

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.520
seeing clusters of infants born with focal melia.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.680
Hands or feet attached directly to the torso

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.640
or limbs entirely absent.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.360
The same compound that had been released to relieve anxiety

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.600
and nausea had instead interfered with limb development

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.380
in the first week's after conception.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.660
Kemi Grunenthal had developed Thalidomide in the early 1950s

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.820
while searching for an inexpensive alternative to barbiturates.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:57.440
At the time, barbiturate overdoses

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.880
were a leading cause of accidental death and suicide in Europe.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.780
A drug that produced sedation without depressing respiration

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.660
appeared to solve that problem.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:10.440
Company pharmacologists tested the compound on rodents

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.100
and observed no lethal dose.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.880
They interpreted this as evidence of unusual safety.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.880
Physicians in post-war Germany facing crowded hospitals

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:23.340
and limited options for treating insomnia and mourning sickness

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.780
welcomed a new agent that could be sold without prescription.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.580
Regulators operated under laws written before the scale

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.700
of synthetic drug effects was understood.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.240
So the absence of obvious toxicity in animals

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.920
was treated as sufficient proof of human safety.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.760
Contragan reached pharmacies in late 1957

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.920
and was soon exported under license to Britain as Dystival,

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.300
Canada as Kevadan, Australia, Japan,

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.240
and more than 20 other countries.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.380
Sales literature emphasized that the drug

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.360
had been given to thousands of patients

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.760
without serious side effects and could safely

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.280
calm expectant mothers.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.440
By 1960, an estimated 1 million people

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.480
were taking Thalidomide daily in West Germany alone.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.980
A few physicians noted peripheral neuritis in long-term users.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.460
These reports circulated slowly and did not halt

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:17.640
over the counter sales.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:21.580
In the United States, Richardson Merrill submitted an application

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.040
to the FDA in 1960.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:27.560
Reviewer Francis Kelsey repeatedly requested

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:31.380
additional safety data, citing the emerging neuritis reports

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:34.500
and the lack of controlled studies on pregnant patients.

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:40.500
Between 1958 and 1962, roughly 10,000 children worldwide

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:43.520
were born with Thalidomide-induced malformations.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:47.100
Another 10 to 20,000 pregnancies are believed

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.320
to have ended in miscarriage or stillbirth.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.860
The drug crossed the placenta during the narrow window

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.000
of day's 20 to 36 after fertilization

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.580
and blocked angiogenesis required for limb bud formation.

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.860
Because the molecule had shown no toxicity

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:06.840
in adult rodents or in short-term human trials,

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.060
no one had examined its effect

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:11.320
on rapidly dividing embryonic tissue.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.140
The first published connection between the drug

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:17.840
and focal milieu appeared in a November 1961 letter

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.960
by German pediatrician Wiedu-Kind Lenz.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.800
By then, the compound had already been taken

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:25.920
by tens of thousands of pregnant women.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.900
In countries where Thalidomide remained available

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:33.020
until early 1962, the rate of limb reduction defects

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.540
rose 10 to 20 fold above baseline.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:39.680
Families faced lifelong medical costs, social stigma

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:44.100
and in some jurisdictions legal barriers to proving causation.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.900
The disaster also revealed how quickly

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.180
a new molecule could move from laboratory

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:52.560
to medicine cabinet when regulators relied primarily

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.040
on manufacturer-submitted animal data.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:59.900
Grunenthal withdrew contra-gon in November 1961.

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.960
Most other markets followed within months.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:06.420
In the United States, Thalidomide was never approved,

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:10.100
sparing American births from the same scale of injury.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:13.400
The episode prompted passage of the 1962

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.600
Kefava Harris amendments, which required proof

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:19.160
of efficacy and more rigorous safety testing

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.020
before marketing.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:24.140
Modern terror to genocide studies, pregnancy registries

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:27.060
and risk evaluation and mitigation strategies

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:30.140
trace their regulatory lineage to that statute.

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:34.640
Survivors in several countries later received compensation funds

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.300
though amounts and eligibility rules varied.

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:40.060
Today, Thalidomide is prescribed

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:43.200
under strict controls for leprosy and certain cancers

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:46.920
with mandatory contraception and monthly testing requirements

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:49.720
that themselves illustrate how later safeguards

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.460
were built on the original failure.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.660
When a new compound shows no toxicity in adult animals,

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:58.240
further investigation is still required

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:01.160
for every stage of human development that might be affected.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:04.720
Regulatory systems that treat absence of evidence

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:08.560
as evidence of safety create an opening for molecules

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:12.500
whose effects appear only under specific biological conditions.

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:15.740
Requiring independent verification of both efficacy

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:19.320
and reproductive safety before widespread use

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:22.720
remains the most direct way to prevent similar scale of harm.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.420
The question for any new therapeutic class is whether

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:28.820
today's data standards would detect an effect

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:32.720
as narrow and devastating as the one Thalidomide produced.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:34.720
We'll leave it there for today.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.880
Thanks for thinking through this one with me.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.820
If you know someone who loves a good cautionary tale,

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:42.620
send it their way and I'll see you tomorrow with another.

